# L §5.3 moves: "Under cuts K ≥ this version's known, V's governs span is SPAN ...; under earlier cuts V keeps
# its own."  V governs 2016-06.. (known 2016-01-01); W (known 2016-02-01) moves V to 2016-01..  Read at
# 2016-03-01: as known 2016-01-15, V governs from 2016-06-01, so no row governs (a hole, L §4.6 step 5);
# under the model's cut (2016-03-01 ≥ W's known) V governs from 2016-01-01 and its row is read.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source s "s"

input n: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2016-06..
  known 2016-01-01
  n = 7

version w
  cite s
  known 2016-02-01
  moves v1 to 2016-01..

ask q1: n law 2016-03-01 as known 2016-01-15
ask q2: n law 2016-03-01
=== expect
q1: ?"n: no value at 2016-03-01" (n)
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-01-15
q2: 7
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-03-01
